_meanings:
.²1 The natural condition or state of anything, nature, natural form (<ab>opp.</ab>
 {#vikfti#} which is a change or effect); {#taM taM niyamamAsTAya prakftyA#}
 {#niyatAH svayA#} <ls>Bg. 7. 20</ls>. {#prakftyA yadvakram#} <ls>Ś. 1. 9</ls>; {#uzRatvamagnyAtapasaMprayogAt#}
 {#SEtyaM hi yat sA prakftirjalasya#} <ls>R. 5. 54</ls>; {#maraRaM prakftiH SarIriRAM#}
 {#vikftirjIvitamucyate buDEH#} <ls>R. 8. 87</ls>; <ls>U. 7. 19</ls>; {#apehi re atraBavAn#}
 {#prakftimApannaH#} <ls>Ś. 2</ls> ‘has resumed his wonted nature’; {#prakftim Apad#}
 or {#pratipad#} or {#prakftO sTA#} ‘to come to oneʼs senses’, ‘regain
 oneʼs consciousness’.
.²2 Natural disposition, temper, temperament, nature, constitution; {#prakftiH#}
 {#Kalu sA mahIyasaH sahate nAnyasamunnatiM yayA#} <ls>Ki. 2. 21</ls>; {#kaTaM gata#}
 {#eva AtmanaH prakftim#} <ls>Ś. 7</ls> ‘natural character’; {#apaSyat pARqavaSrezwo#}
 {#harzeRa prakftiM gataH#} <ls>Mb. 39. 66</ls> (<ab>com.</ab> {#prakftiM svAsTyam#}); so {#prakftikfpaRa#},
 {#prakftisidDaH#} see below.
.²3 Make, form, figure; {#mahAnuBAvaprakftiH#} <ls>Māl. 1</ls>.
.²4 Extraction, descent; {#gopAlaprakftirAryako'smi#} <ls>Mk. 7</ls>.
.²5 Origin, source, original or material cause, the material of which anything
 is made; {#nArTAnAM prakftiM vetsi#} <ls>Mb. 4. 49. 1</ls>; {#prakftiScopAdAnakAraRaM#}
 {#ca brahmAByupagantavyam#} <ls>Ś. B.</ls> (see the full discussion on <ls>Br. Sūt. 1. 4. 23</ls>);
 {#yAmAhuH sarvaBUtaprakftiriti#} <ls>Ś. 1. 1</ls>; <ls>Bhāg. 4. 28. 24</ls>.
.²6 (In <ab>Sāṅ. phil.</ab>) Nature (as distinguished from {#puruza#}), the original
 source of the material world, consisting of the three essential qualities
 {#sattva, rajas#} and {#tamas#}. It is also mentioned as one of the four
 contentments; {#prakftyupAdAnakAlaBAgAKyAH#} <ls>Sāṅ. K. 50</ls>.
.²7 (In <ab>gram.</ab>) The radical or crude form of a word to which case-terminations
 and other affixes are applied; {#prakftipratyayayorivAnubanDaH#} <ls>Ki. 13. 19</ls>.
.²8 A model, pattern, standard, (especially in ritualistic works); <ls>Bhāg. 5. 7. 5</ls>.
.²9 A woman.
.²10 The personified will of the Supreme Spirit in the creation (identified
 with {#mAyA#} or illusion); {#mayADyakzeRa prakftiH sUyate sacarAcaram#} <ls>Bg. 9. 10</ls>.
.²11 The male or female organ of generation.
.²12 A mother.
.²13 (In <ab>arith.</ab>) A coefficient, or multiplier.
.²14 (In anatomy) Temperament of the humours; {#prakftiM yAnti BUtAni nigrahaH#}
 {#kiM karizyati#} <ls>Bg. 3. 33</ls>.
.²15 An animal.
.²16 An artisan.
.²17 The Supreme Being; {#na hyasti sarvaBUtezu duHKamasmin kutaH suKam .#}
 {#evaM prakftiBUtAnAM sarvasaMsargayAyinAm ..#} <ls>Mb. 12. 152. 16</ls>.
.²18 Eight forms of the Supreme Being; {#BUmirApo'nalo vAyuH KaM mano#}
 {#budDireva ca . ahaMkAra itIyaM me BinnA prakfti-razwaDA ..#} <ls>Bg. 7. 4</ls>.

.²19 The way of life ({#jIvana#}); {#satAM vE dadato'nnaM ca loke'smin#}
 {#prakftirDruvA#} <ls>Mb. 12. 18. 27</ls>. (<ab>pl.</ab>)
.²1 A kingʼs ministers, the body of ministers or counsellors, ministry;
 {#aTAnATAH prakftayo mAtfbanDunivAsinam#} <ls>R. 12. 12</ls>; <ls>Pt. 1. 48</ls>; {#aSudDaprakftO#}
 {#rAjYi janatA nAnurajyate#} <ls n="Pt. 1.">301</ls>.
.²2 The subjects (of a king); {#pravartatAM prakftihitAya pArTivaH#} <ls>Ś. 7. 35</ls>;
 {#nfpatiH prakftIravekzitum#} <ls>R. 8. 18</ls>, <ls n="R. 8.">10</ls>.
.²3 The constituent elements of the state ({#saptANgAni#}), {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%}
.²1 the king;
.²2 the minister;
.²3 the allies;
.²4 treasure;
.²5 army;
.²6 territory;
.²7 fortresses <ab>&c.</ab>; and the corporations of citizens (which is sometimes
 added to the 7); {#svAmyamAtyasuhftkoSarAzwradurgabalAni ca#} <ls>Ak.</ls>
.²4 The various sovereigns to be considered in case of war; (for full explanation
 see <ls>Kull.</ls> on <ls>Ms. 7. 155</ls> and 157).
.²5 The eight primary elements out of which everything else is evolved
 according to the Sāṅkhyas; see <ls>Sāṅ. K. 3</ls>.
.²6 The five primary elements of creations ({#paYcamahABUtAni#}) {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%}
 {#pfTvI, ap, tejas, vAyu#} and {#AkASa#}; {#prakftiM te Bajizyanti nazwaprakftayo#}
 {#mayi#} <ls>Mb. 5. 73. 17</ls>.

a minister, a functionary (of the state); {#jAnAmi tvAM#}
 {#prakftipuruzaM kAmarUpaM maGonaH#} <ls>Me. 6</ls>.
.²2 a standard or model of a man.
